Cell["What is new, and what is reused", "Section",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],

Cell["\<\
Luis Perez Morales and Claude (Fable 5.1) proved that every finite \
perturbation of the period-three ether erodes into an initially matching \
prefix, and that there is no finite ether wall of any width (submission \
R30-20261024-1fc962, kit PR #10). Their proof follows the first defect. Of \
its 24 local states, 23 have a decreasing potential. A run of the remaining \
bad state advances by at least eight columns per step, whereas the rightmost \
defect moves by one.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A white tail is an infinite perturbation of the ether, with no rightmost \
defect. The new ",
 Cell[BoxData["erosion_bounded"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 " needs only a defect witness at a position at most R+(t-T) for every t>=T. \
The first defect cannot exceed that witness. The earlier bad-state and \
potential arguments then apply. A white tail supplies R=W+12: its support \
grows at most one cell per step, and among the next twelve ether cells there \
is a black cell. The bound twelve is convenient, not claimed optimal. This \
changes the permitted right sides, with no finite width or temporal-clock \
limit."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],

Cell["\<\
PR #11 contains the new catalog module and explicitly depends on #10. The \
source below carries both proofs because #10 is not installed in the current \
reference kit. The earlier proof, its certificate and its potential remain \
credited to their original authors. No priority claim is made for those \
results.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],

Cell["An explicit driven evolution", "Section",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],

Cell["\<\
The boundary here is imposed externally. The image shows the difference from \
the matching ether for a finite right word; the initially matching prefix has \
length fourteen, and first departs at time twenty-four. This is one \
illustration, not the proof of the unbounded quantifiers.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"etherColumns", "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"IntegerDigits", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"FromDigits", "[", 
        RowBox[{"#", ",", "2"}], "]"}], ",", "2", ",", "3"}], "]"}], "&"}], 
    " ", "/@", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<001\>\"", ",", "\"\<001\>\"", ",", "\"\<011\>\"", 
      ",", "\"\<110\>\"", ",", "\"\<010\>\"", ",", "\"\<010\>\"", 
      ",", "\"\<110\>\"", ",", "\"\<101\>\"", ",", "\"\<100\>\"", 
      ",", "\"\<100\>\"", ",", "\"\<101\>\"", ",", "\"\<011\>\""}], "}"}]}]}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ether", "[", 
    RowBox[{"j_", ",", "t_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"etherColumns", "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Mod", "[", 
        RowBox[{"j", ",", "12"}], "]"}], "+", "1"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Mod", "[", 
        RowBox[{"t", ",", "3"}], "]"}], "+", "1"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"halfStep", "[", 
    RowBox[{"a_", ",", "b_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"BitXor", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"BitOr", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"BitShiftLeft", "[", 
        RowBox[{"a", ",", "1"}], "]"}], ",", "b"}], "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"BitOr", "[", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", 
       RowBox[{"BitShiftRight", "[", 
        RowBox[{"a", ",", "1"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"exampleRows", "=", 
   RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"halfStep", "[", 
       RowBox[{"#1", ",", 
        RowBox[{"ether", "[", 
         RowBox[{"4", ",", "#2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "&"}], ",", 
     "17619461964066119253545154634814", ",", 
     RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "39"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"exampleDifference", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"BitXor", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"BitAnd", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"BitShiftRight", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"exampleRows", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"t", "+", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
           RowBox[{"p", "-", "1"}]}], "]"}], ",", "1"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
       "  ", 
       RowBox[{"ether", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"4", "+", "p"}], ",", "t"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "40"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"p", ",", "1", ",", "120"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ArrayPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{"exampleDifference", ",", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", "->", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", "->", "Large"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", 
    "->", "\"\<Black marks a defect from the ether; the first fourteen \
columns depart at time 24\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->1347158791,ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],

