 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The source contains the unchanged mathematical proof bodies of PR #10 at \
f6885abec122a9dcbb3160cb69312323bc075dc1 and of the new module at \
765143dc2bf6d4b85f91df3a60433d80ae30ff85. Only their module/import/export \
wrappers are removed for this single-file environment. Three named aliases \
expose the new claims under ",
 Cell[BoxData["Rule30Submission"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 ". No unmerged module is imported."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`LeanLink`\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$Rule30PrizeKit", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Environment", "[", "\"\<RULE30PRIZE_KIT\>\"", "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"rule30Submission", "=", 
  RowBox[{"LeanImportString", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<import Rule30PrizeKit\\nimport \
Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30Prize\\nimport \
Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30EtherThree\\n\\n/-!\\n# Rule 30, least \
period 3: the ether erodes, so there is no wall of any width\\n\\n**Partial \
result.** Setting of `Rule30EtherThree`: `F` is a rule-30 evolution of the \
columns\\n`p \[GreaterEqual] 1` (`IsR30 F`) whose column `0` is ether column \
`j0` with phase offset `s` from time `t1` on.\\nThe ether value of column `p` \
at time `t` is `ether3 (j0 + p) (t + s)`.\\n\\n* `erosion3_fin`: if at time \
`t1` the columns `1..k` carry the ether, the columns beyond `k + w`\\n  carry \
the ether, and some column does not, then at some time `t \[LessEqual] t1 + 3 \
w + 6` one of the\\n  columns `1..k` differs from the ether. A finite \
perturbation always eats into the ether, at\\n  average speed at least `2/5` \
once it is in its wake.\\n* `no_wall`: for every attachment column `a` and \
every width `b \[GreaterEqual] 1`, a predicate `W` with\\n  `WallOK a b W` is \
empty. This extends the kernel certificate `no_wall_le_12`\\n  \
(`Rule30EtherThreeNoWall`) from widths `\[LessEqual] 12` to all widths. So \
the period-3 ether-and-wall\\n  family of `Rule30EtherThree` is empty, and \
`absorption3_excludes` is vacuous for every wall:\\n  the ether-and-wall \
route to least period 3 is closed. The open statements for least period 3\\n  \
(`AbsorptionT t001`, `Q001`, `C3s001`, `C3w(011)`) do not involve walls and \
remain open.\\n\\n**The argument.** Let the *front* `D` be the leftmost \
column that differs from the ether\\n(`Front`). Its *state* is the class of \
column `D`, `(j0 + D + 4 (t + s)) mod 12` (`cls`), together\\nwith whether \
column `D + 1` is also a defect (`ubit`): 24 states. Columns `D - 2, D - 1` \
are ether,\\nso the next front and its state depend only on the class and on \
the columns `D + 1 .. D + 4`.\\nA kernel check over these 576 local patterns \
(`cert_all`) shows:\\n\\n* exactly one state, `B = (class 10, D + 1 \
defective)`, can send the front three or more columns to\\n  the right in one \
step; every other next front lies in `D - 1 .. D + 2` and is not `B`;\\n* \
from `B` the front either moves by exactly `+2` into a good state, or jumps \
right by `\[GreaterEqual] 3`;\\n  if it lands in `B` again, the class \
equation forces a jump of at least `8`;\\n* a potential `\[Psi] \[Element] \
[0, 10]` on the 23 good states (`psiTab`) satisfies\\n  `5 \[CapitalDelta]D + \
2 + \[Psi](new) \[LessEqual] \[Psi](old)` on every step from a good state.\\n\
\\n`front_step` turns this into a statement about `F` (for `D \[GreaterEqual] \
2`; column `0` is forced, not\\ncomputed). Hence the good states are closed \
and `5 D + 2 t + \[Psi]` does not increase (`wake_good`):\\nthe front moves \
left at average speed at least `2/5`. For a finite perturbation the rightmost\
\\ndefect `R` moves right by exactly one column per step (`redge_step`: rule \
30 is permutive in its\\nleft input) and `D \[LessEqual] R`. A `B \
\[RightArrow] B` step gains `\[GreaterEqual] 8` on `R`'s `1`, so the initial \
run of `B` steps\\nis shorter than `(R - D) / 7 + 1 \[LessEqual] (w - 1) / 7 \
+ 1` (`run_bad`); after it the front is good and at\\nmost `w + n + 1` \
columns right of `k`, and the potential brings it to `\[LessEqual] k` in \
time. The arithmetic\\ngives `3 w + 6`.\\n\\nFor `no_wall`: from a wall state \
at phase `< 3`, put the ether on columns `1..k`\\n(`k \[Congruent] a mod \
12`), the strip on `k + 1 .. k + b`, a flipped cell at `k + b + 1` and the \
ether beyond\\n(`wallCfg`), and drive column `0` with the ether \
(`Rule30Ether.drv`). `trap_invariant3` keeps\\ncolumns `1..k` ether forever, \
and `erosion3_fin` (with `w = b + 1`) breaks them.\\n\\nThe certificate and \
the potential come from an exhaustive computation (two independent \
code\\npaths); here they are checked by the kernel (`decide +kernel`, about \
two seconds).\\n\\n**Source.** Luis Perez Morales and Claude (Fable 5.1), \
Rule 30 Prize submission\\n`R30-20261024-1fc962`, ported to core \
Lean.\\n-/\\n\\n\\n\\nnamespace Ruliology.CellularAutomata\\nnamespace \
Rule30EtherThree\\n\\nopen Rule30Jen Rule30Ether\\n\\n/-! ### The local \
certificate -/\\n\\n/-- The potential `\[Psi]` on front states `(class, next \
column defective)`. -/\\ndef psiTab (g : Nat) (u : Bool) : Nat :=\\n  (if u \
then [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 0, 7, 2, 3, 0, 2] else [0, 1, 2, 0, 10, 5, 6, 7, 8, \
9, 4, 5]).getD g 0\\n\\n/-- The single bad front state `B = (class 10, next \
column defective)`. -/\\ndef isBad (g : Nat) (u : Bool) : Bool := g == 10 && \
u\\n\\n/-- New cells at columns `D - 1 + i` (`i \[LessEqual] 4`) when columns \
`D - 2, D - 1` carry the ether, column `D`\\nis a defect, and columns `D + 1 \
.. D + 4` are `x1 .. x4`; column `D` is ether column `c`, phase \
`\[CurlyPhi]`. -/\\ndef nC (c \[CurlyPhi] : Nat) (x1 x2 x3 x4 : Bool) : Nat \
\[RightArrow] Bool\\n  | 0 => rule (ether3 (c + 10) \[CurlyPhi]) (ether3 (c + \
11) \[CurlyPhi]) (!ether3 c \[CurlyPhi])\\n  | 1 => rule (ether3 (c + 11) \
\[CurlyPhi]) (!ether3 c \[CurlyPhi]) x1\\n  | 2 => rule (!ether3 c \
\[CurlyPhi]) x1 x2\\n  | 3 => rule x1 x2 x3\\n  | _ => rule x2 x3 x4\\n\\n/-- \
Whether the new cell at column `D - 1 + i` is a defect. -/\\ndef dC (c \
\[CurlyPhi] : Nat) (x1 x2 x3 x4 : Bool) (i : Nat) : Bool :=\\n  nC c \
\[CurlyPhi] x1 x2 x3 x4 i != ether3 (c + 11 + i) (\[CurlyPhi] + 1)\\n\\n/-- \
Whether column `D + 1` is a defect. -/\\ndef uC (c \[CurlyPhi] : Nat) (x1 : \
Bool) : Bool := x1 != ether3 (c + 1) \[CurlyPhi]\\n\\n/-- The new front `D - \
1 + i` is good, and the potential drops. -/\\nabbrev stepGood (c \[CurlyPhi] \
: Nat) (x1 x2 x3 x4 : Bool) (i : Nat) : Prop :=\\n  isBad ((c + 4 * \
\[CurlyPhi] + i + 3) % 12) (dC c \[CurlyPhi] x1 x2 x3 x4 (i + 1)) = false \
\[And]\\n  (isBad ((c + 4 * \[CurlyPhi]) % 12) (uC c \[CurlyPhi] x1) = true \
\[RightArrow] i = 3) \[And]\\n  (isBad ((c + 4 * \[CurlyPhi]) % 12) (uC c \
\[CurlyPhi] x1) = false \[RightArrow]\\n    5 * i + 2 + psiTab ((c + 4 * \
\[CurlyPhi] + i + 3) % 12) (dC c \[CurlyPhi] x1 x2 x3 x4 (i + 1)) \
\[LessEqual]\\n      psiTab ((c + 4 * \[CurlyPhi]) % 12) (uC c \[CurlyPhi] \
x1) + 5)\\n\\n/-- The certificate for one local pattern. -/\\nabbrev certAt \
(c \[CurlyPhi] : Nat) (x1 x2 x3 x4 : Bool) : Prop :=\\n  (\[ForAll] i, i < 4 \
\[RightArrow] (\[ForAll] j, j < i \[RightArrow] dC c \[CurlyPhi] x1 x2 x3 x4 \
j = false) \[RightArrow] dC c \[CurlyPhi] x1 x2 x3 x4 i = true \
\[RightArrow]\\n    stepGood c \[CurlyPhi] x1 x2 x3 x4 i) \[And]\\n  ((\
\[ForAll] j, j < 4 \[RightArrow] dC c \[CurlyPhi] x1 x2 x3 x4 j = false) \
\[RightArrow] isBad ((c + 4 * \[CurlyPhi]) % 12) (uC c \[CurlyPhi] x1) = \
true)\\n\\nset_option synthInstance.maxSize 1024 in\\nset_option \
synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000 in\\n/-- **The local certificate** (12 \
ether columns \[Times] 3 phases \[Times] 16 right patterns = 576 cases). \
-/\\ntheorem cert_all : \[ForAll] c, c < 12 \[RightArrow] \[ForAll] \
\[CurlyPhi], \[CurlyPhi] < 3 \[RightArrow] \[ForAll] x1 x2 x3 x4 : Bool, \
certAt c \[CurlyPhi] x1 x2 x3 x4 := by\\n  decide +kernel\\n\\ntheorem \
psiTab_le : \[ForAll] g, g < 12 \[RightArrow] \[ForAll] u, psiTab g u \
\[LessEqual] 10 := by decide\\n\\n/-! ### Fronts of an evolution \
-/\\n\\nsection\\nvariable (F : Nat \[RightArrow] Nat \[RightArrow] Bool) (j0 \
s : Nat)\\n\\n/-- The ether value at column `p`, time `t`. -/\\ndef eth (j0 s \
p t : Nat) : Bool := ether3 (j0 + p) (t + s)\\n\\n/-- `D` is the front at \
time `t`: columns `0 .. D - 1` are ether, column `D` is not. -/\\ndef Front \
(t D : Nat) : Prop := (\[ForAll] p, p < D \[RightArrow] F t p = eth j0 s p t) \
\[And] F t D \[NotEqual] eth j0 s D t\\n\\n/-- `R` is the right edge at time \
`t`: column `R` is a defect and every column right of it is ether. -/\\ndef \
REdge (t R : Nat) : Prop := F t R \[NotEqual] eth j0 s R t \[And] \[ForAll] \
p, R < p \[RightArrow] F t p = eth j0 s p t\\n\\n/-- The class of column `D` \
at time `t`. -/\\ndef cls (D t : Nat) : Nat := (j0 + D + 4 * (t + s)) % 12\\n\
\\n/-- Whether column `D + 1` is a defect at time `t`. -/\\ndef ubit (t D : \
Nat) : Bool := F t (D + 1) != eth j0 s (D + 1) t\\n\\n/-- The front state at \
`(t, D)` is the bad state `B`. -/\\ndef IsB (t D : Nat) : Prop := isBad (cls \
j0 s D t) (ubit F j0 s t D) = true\\n\\n/-- The potential of the front state. \
-/\\ndef psiF (t D : Nat) : Nat := psiTab (cls j0 s D t) (ubit F j0 s t D)\\n\
\\nend\\n\\ntheorem eth_rule (j0 s q t : Nat) :\\n    eth j0 s (q + 1) (t + \
1) = rule (eth j0 s q t) (eth j0 s (q + 1) t) (eth j0 s (q + 2) t) := by\\n  \
unfold eth\\n  rw [show t + 1 + s = (t + s) + 1 by omega, ether3_rule,\\n    \
ether3_congr (j := j0 + (q + 1) + 11) (j' := j0 + q) (by omega) rfl,\\n    \
show j0 + (q + 1) + 1 = j0 + (q + 2) by omega]\\n\\ntheorem rule_flip (a b c \
: Bool) : rule (!a) b c = !rule a b c := by\\n  cases a <;> cases b <;> cases \
c <;> rfl\\n\\ntheorem ne_eth {a b : Bool} (h : a \[NotEqual] b) : a = !b := \
by cases a <;> cases b <;> simp_all\\n\\ntheorem psiF_le (F : Nat \
\[RightArrow] Nat \[RightArrow] Bool) (j0 s t D : Nat) : psiF F j0 s t D \
\[LessEqual] 10 :=\\n  psiTab_le _ (Nat.mod_lt _ (by decide)) _\\n\\ntheorem \
isB_cls {F : Nat \[RightArrow] Nat \[RightArrow] Bool} {j0 s t D : Nat} (h : \
IsB F j0 s t D) : cls j0 s D t = 10 := by\\n  unfold IsB isBad at h\\n  simp \
only [Bool.and_eq_true, beq_iff_eq] at h\\n  exact h.1\\n\\n/-- The ether \
prefix shrinks by at most one column per step. -/\\ntheorem prefix_step {F : \
Nat \[RightArrow] Nat \[RightArrow] Bool} (hF : IsR30 F) {j0 s t D : Nat}\\n  \
  (h0 : F (t + 1) 0 = eth j0 s 0 (t + 1)) (hpre : \[ForAll] p, p < D \
\[RightArrow] F t p = eth j0 s p t) :\\n    \[ForAll] p, p + 1 < D \
\[RightArrow] F (t + 1) p = eth j0 s p (t + 1) := by\\n  intro p hp\\n  \
rcases p with _ | q\\n  \[CenterDot] exact h0\\n  \[CenterDot] rw [hF t q, \
eth_rule, hpre q (by omega), hpre (q + 1) (by omega), hpre (q + 2) (by \
omega)]\\n\\n/-- **The right edge moves right by exactly one column per \
step** (rule 30 is permutive in its left input). -/\\ntheorem redge_step {F : \
Nat \[RightArrow] Nat \[RightArrow] Bool} (hF : IsR30 F) {j0 s t R : Nat} (h \
: REdge F j0 s t R) :\\n    REdge F j0 s (t + 1) (R + 1) := by\\n  refine \
\:27e8?_, fun p hp => ?_\:27e9\\n  \[CenterDot] rw [hF t R, eth_rule, ne_eth \
h.1, h.2 (R + 1) (by omega), h.2 (R + 2) (by omega), rule_flip]\\n    cases \
rule (eth j0 s R t) (eth j0 s (R + 1) t) (eth j0 s (R + 2) t) <;> decide\\n  \
\[CenterDot] obtain \:27e8q, rfl\:27e9 : \[Exists] q, p = q + 1 := \:27e8p - \
1, by omega\:27e9\\n    rw [hF t q, eth_rule, h.2 q (by omega), h.2 (q + 1) \
(by omega), h.2 (q + 2) (by omega)]\\n\\ntheorem redge_add {F : Nat \
\[RightArrow] Nat \[RightArrow] Bool} (hF : IsR30 F) {j0 s t R : Nat} (h : \
REdge F j0 s t R) :\\n    \[ForAll] n, REdge F j0 s (t + n) (R + n)\\n  | 0 \
=> h\\n  | n + 1 => redge_step hF (redge_add hF h n)\\n\\ntheorem \
front_le_redge {F : Nat \[RightArrow] Nat \[RightArrow] Bool} {j0 s t D R : \
Nat} (hD : Front F j0 s t D)\\n    (hR : REdge F j0 s t R) : D \[LessEqual] R \
:= by\\n  refine Nat.le_of_not_lt fun h => hR.1 (hD.1 R h)\\n\\n/-- A least \
witness (core Lean only). -/\\ntheorem exists_least {P : Nat \[RightArrow] \
Prop} (n : Nat) (hn : P n) : \[Exists] m, P m \[And] \[ForAll] q, q < m \
\[RightArrow] \[Not] P q := by\\n  induction n using Nat.strongRecOn with\\n  \
| ind n ih =>\\n    by_cases h : \[Exists] q, q < n \[And] P q\\n    \
\[CenterDot] obtain \:27e8q, hq, hPq\:27e9 := h; exact ih q hq hPq\\n    \
\[CenterDot] exact \:27e8n, hn, fun q hq hPq => h \:27e8q, hq, \
hPq\:27e9\:27e9\\n\\n/-- **One step of the front** (certified by `cert_all`). \
Assumes the front is at `D \[GreaterEqual] 2` (column `0`\\nis forced, so the \
local relaxation is only valid there) and that some defect exists at `t + 1`.\
\\nFrom a good state the next state is good and `5 D + \[Psi]` drops by at \
least `2`; from `B` the front\\neither moves by exactly `+2` into a good \
state or jumps right by at least `3`. -/\\ntheorem front_step {F : Nat \
\[RightArrow] Nat \[RightArrow] Bool} (hF : IsR30 F) {j0 s t D : Nat}\\n    \
(h0 : F (t + 1) 0 = eth j0 s 0 (t + 1)) (hD2 : 2 \[LessEqual] D) (hfr : Front \
F j0 s t D)\\n    (hex : \[Exists] p, F (t + 1) p \[NotEqual] eth j0 s p (t + \
1)) :\\n    \[Exists] D', Front F j0 s (t + 1) D' \[And] D \[LessEqual] D' + \
1 \[And]\\n      ((\[Not] IsB F j0 s t D \[And] \[Not] IsB F j0 s (t + 1) D' \
\[And]\\n          5 * D' + 2 + psiF F j0 s (t + 1) D' \[LessEqual] 5 * D + \
psiF F j0 s t D) \[Or]\\n        (IsB F j0 s t D \[And] \[Not] IsB F j0 s (t \
+ 1) D' \[And] D' = D + 2) \[Or]\\n        (IsB F j0 s t D \[And] D + 3 \
\[LessEqual] D')) := by\\n  classical\\n  obtain \:27e8E, rfl\:27e9 : \
\[Exists] E, D = E + 2 := \:27e8D - 2, by omega\:27e9\\n  obtain \:27e8c, hc\
\:27e9 : \[Exists] c, c = (j0 + (E + 2)) % 12 := \:27e8_, rfl\:27e9\\n  \
obtain \:27e8\[CurlyPhi], h\[CurlyPhi]\:27e9 : \[Exists] \[CurlyPhi], \
\[CurlyPhi] = (t + s) % 3 := \:27e8_, rfl\:27e9\\n  -- the row at time `t`\\n \
 have x0 : F t E = ether3 (c + 10) \[CurlyPhi] := by\\n    rw [hfr.1 E (by \
omega)]; exact ether3_congr (by omega) (by omega)\\n  have x1 : F t (E + 1) = \
ether3 (c + 11) \[CurlyPhi] := by\\n    rw [hfr.1 (E + 1) (by omega)]; exact \
ether3_congr (by omega) (by omega)\\n  have x2 : F t (E + 2) = !ether3 c \
\[CurlyPhi] := by\\n    rw [ne_eth hfr.2, show eth j0 s (E + 2) t = ether3 c \
\[CurlyPhi] from ether3_congr (by omega) (by omega)]\\n  generalize hy1 : F t \
(E + 3) = y1\\n  generalize hy2 : F t (E + 4) = y2\\n  generalize hy3 : F t \
(E + 5) = y3\\n  generalize hy4 : F t (E + 6) = y4\\n  -- the row at time `t \
+ 1`\\n  have hn : \[ForAll] i, i \[LessEqual] 4 \[RightArrow] F (t + 1) (E + \
1 + i) = nC c \[CurlyPhi] y1 y2 y3 y4 i := by\\n    intro i hi\\n    have hr \
:= hF t (E + i)\\n    rw [show E + i + 1 = E + 1 + i by omega] at hr\\n    rw \
[hr]\\n    rcases (by omega : i = 0 \[Or] i = 1 \[Or] i = 2 \[Or] i = 3 \[Or] \
i = 4) with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl\\n    \[CenterDot] simp only \
[Nat.add_zero]; rw [x0, x1, x2]; rfl\\n    \[CenterDot] rw [show E + 1 + 1 = \
E + 2 by omega, show E + 1 + 2 = E + 3 by omega, x1, x2, hy1]; rfl\\n    \
\[CenterDot] rw [show E + 2 + 1 = E + 3 by omega, show E + 2 + 2 = E + 4 by \
omega, x2, hy1, hy2]; rfl\\n    \[CenterDot] rw [show E + 3 + 1 = E + 4 by \
omega, show E + 3 + 2 = E + 5 by omega, hy1, hy2, hy3]; rfl\\n    \
\[CenterDot] rw [show E + 4 + 1 = E + 5 by omega, show E + 4 + 2 = E + 6 by \
omega, hy2, hy3, hy4]; rfl\\n  have he : \[ForAll] i, eth j0 s (E + 1 + i) (t \
+ 1) = ether3 (c + 11 + i) (\[CurlyPhi] + 1) :=\\n    fun i => ether3_congr \
(by omega) (by omega)\\n  have hd : \[ForAll] i, i \[LessEqual] 4 \
\[RightArrow]\\n      (dC c \[CurlyPhi] y1 y2 y3 y4 i = true \
\[LeftRightArrow] F (t + 1) (E + 1 + i) \[NotEqual] eth j0 s (E + 1 + i) (t + \
1)) := by\\n    intro i hi\\n    unfold dC; rw [hn i hi, he i, bne_iff_ne]\\n \
 -- the front state at time `t`\\n  have hcls : cls j0 s (E + 2) t = (c + 4 * \
\[CurlyPhi]) % 12 := by unfold cls; omega\\n  have hub : ubit F j0 s t (E + \
2) = uC c \[CurlyPhi] y1 := by\\n    unfold ubit uC\\n    rw [show E + 2 + 1 \
= E + 3 by omega, hy1,\\n      show eth j0 s (E + 3) t = ether3 (c + 1) \
\[CurlyPhi] from ether3_congr (by omega) (by omega)]\\n  -- the new front\\n  \
obtain \:27e8D', hsp, hmin\:27e9 : \[Exists] D', F (t + 1) D' \[NotEqual] eth \
j0 s D' (t + 1) \[And]\\n      \[ForAll] p, p < D' \[RightArrow] F (t + 1) p \
= eth j0 s p (t + 1) :=\\n    by\\n      obtain \:27e8p0, hp0\:27e9 := hex\\n \
     obtain \:27e8m, hm, hmin\:27e9 := exists_least (P := fun p => F (t + 1) \
p \[NotEqual] eth j0 s p (t + 1)) p0 hp0\\n      exact \:27e8m, hm, fun p hp \
=> Classical.not_not.1 (hmin p hp)\:27e9\\n  have hpre := prefix_step hF h0 \
hfr.1\\n  have hD'1 : E + 1 \[LessEqual] D' := by\\n    refine \
Nat.le_of_not_lt fun h => hsp (hpre D' (by omega))\\n  obtain \:27e8i, rfl\
\:27e9 : \[Exists] i, D' = E + 1 + i := \:27e8D' - (E + 1), by omega\:27e9\\n \
 refine \:27e8E + 1 + i, \:27e8hmin, hsp\:27e9, by omega, ?_\:27e9\\n  have \
hbefore : \[ForAll] j, j < i \[RightArrow] j \[LessEqual] 4 \[RightArrow] dC \
c \[CurlyPhi] y1 y2 y3 y4 j = false := by\\n    intro j hj hj4\\n    cases h \
: dC c \[CurlyPhi] y1 y2 y3 y4 j\\n    \[CenterDot] rfl\\n    \[CenterDot] \
exact absurd (hmin (E + 1 + j) (by omega)) ((hd j hj4).1 h)\\n  have cert := \
cert_all c (by omega) \[CurlyPhi] (by omega) y1 y2 y3 y4\\n  have hIsB : IsB \
F j0 s t (E + 2) \[LeftRightArrow] isBad ((c + 4 * \[CurlyPhi]) % 12) (uC c \
\[CurlyPhi] y1) = true := by\\n    unfold IsB; rw [hcls, hub]\\n  by_cases \
hi4 : i < 4\\n  \[CenterDot] have hdi : dC c \[CurlyPhi] y1 y2 y3 y4 i = true \
:= (hd i (by omega)).2 hsp\\n    have hg := cert.1 i hi4 (fun j hj => hbefore \
j hj (by omega)) hdi\\n    have hcls' : cls j0 s (E + 1 + i) (t + 1) = (c + 4 \
* \[CurlyPhi] + i + 3) % 12 := by unfold cls; omega\\n    have hub' : ubit F \
j0 s (t + 1) (E + 1 + i) = dC c \[CurlyPhi] y1 y2 y3 y4 (i + 1) := by\\n      \
unfold ubit dC\\n      rw [show E + 1 + i + 1 = E + 1 + (i + 1) by omega, hn \
(i + 1) (by omega), he (i + 1),\\n        show c + 11 + (i + 1) = c + 11 + (i \
+ 1) from rfl]\\n    have hnB' : \[Not] IsB F j0 s (t + 1) (E + 1 + i) := \
by\\n      unfold IsB; rw [hcls', hub', hg.1]; decide\\n    by_cases hB : \
isBad ((c + 4 * \[CurlyPhi]) % 12) (uC c \[CurlyPhi] y1) = true\\n    \
\[CenterDot] exact Or.inr (Or.inl \:27e8hIsB.2 hB, hnB', by have := hg.2.1 \
hB; omega\:27e9)\\n    \[CenterDot] refine Or.inl \:27e8fun h => hB (hIsB.1 \
h), hnB', ?_\:27e9\\n      have hp := hg.2.2 (by simpa using hB)\\n      \
unfold psiF; rw [hcls', hub', hcls, hub]\\n      omega\\n  \[CenterDot] have \
hB := cert.2 (fun j hj => hbefore j (by omega) (by omega))\\n    exact Or.inr \
(Or.inr \:27e8hIsB.2 hB, by omega\:27e9)\\n\\n/-! ### The good set is closed, \
and the front erodes at speed `2/5` in it -/\\n\\n/-- **(a) The wake.** Once \
the front state is good it stays good, and `5 D + 2 n + \[Psi]` \
never\\nincreases, until the front reaches a column `\[LessEqual] k`. This \
holds for any right side, as long as a\\ndefect exists at every time. \
-/\\ntheorem wake_good {F : Nat \[RightArrow] Nat \[RightArrow] Bool} (hF : \
IsR30 F) {j0 s t1 k : Nat} (hk : 1 \[LessEqual] k)\\n    (h0 : \[ForAll] t, \
t1 \[LessEqual] t \[RightArrow] F t 0 = eth j0 s 0 t)\\n    (hex : \[ForAll] \
t, t1 \[LessEqual] t \[RightArrow] \[Exists] p, F t p \[NotEqual] eth j0 s p \
t) :\\n    \[ForAll] n t D, t1 \[LessEqual] t \[RightArrow] Front F j0 s t D \
\[RightArrow] \[Not] IsB F j0 s t D \[RightArrow]\\n      (\[Exists] t', t \
\[LessEqual] t' \[And] t' \[LessEqual] t + n \[And] \[Exists] p, 1 \
\[LessEqual] p \[And] p \[LessEqual] k \[And] F t' p \[NotEqual] eth j0 s p \
t') \[Or]\\n      (\[Exists] D', Front F j0 s (t + n) D' \[And] \[Not] IsB F \
j0 s (t + n) D' \[And]\\n        5 * D' + 2 * n + psiF F j0 s (t + n) D' \
\[LessEqual] 5 * D + psiF F j0 s t D) := by\\n  intro n\\n  induction n \
with\\n  | zero =>\\n    intro t D _ hD hB\\n    refine Or.inr \:27e8D, hD, \
hB, ?_\:27e9\\n    show 5 * D + 2 * 0 + psiF F j0 s t D \[LessEqual] _\\n    \
omega\\n  | succ n ih =>\\n    intro t D ht hD hB\\n    rcases ih t D ht hD \
hB with \:27e8t', h1, h2, hp\:27e9 | \:27e8D', hD', hB', hpot\:27e9\\n    \
\[CenterDot] exact Or.inl \:27e8t', h1, by omega, hp\:27e9\\n    \[CenterDot] \
by_cases hDk : D' \[LessEqual] k\\n      \[CenterDot] refine Or.inl \:27e8t + \
n, by omega, by omega, D', ?_, hDk, hD'.2\:27e9\\n        refine \
Nat.pos_of_ne_zero fun h => hD'.2 ?_\\n        subst h; exact h0 (t + n) (by \
omega)\\n      \[CenterDot] obtain \:27e8D'', hD'', -, h | h | h\:27e9 :=\\n  \
        front_step hF (h0 (t + n + 1) (by omega)) (by omega) hD' (hex (t + n \
+ 1) (by omega))\\n        \[CenterDot] refine Or.inr \:27e8D'', ?_, ?_, ?_\
\:27e9\\n          \[CenterDot] rw [show t + (n + 1) = t + n + 1 by omega]; \
exact hD''\\n          \[CenterDot] rw [show t + (n + 1) = t + n + 1 by \
omega]; exact h.2.1\\n          \[CenterDot] rw [show t + (n + 1) = t + n + 1 \
by omega]; omega\\n        \[CenterDot] exact absurd h.1 hB'\\n        \
\[CenterDot] exact absurd h.1 hB'\\n\\n/-! ### (b) The bad state: a run of \
`B` steps is short -/\\n\\n/-- From `B`, while `R - D < 7 m`, the front \
reaches a good state within `m` steps: each `B \[RightArrow] B`\\nstep moves \
the front right by at least `8` (class equation), while the right edge moves \
by `1`. -/\\ntheorem run_bad {F : Nat \[RightArrow] Nat \[RightArrow] Bool} \
(hF : IsR30 F) {j0 s t1 : Nat}\\n    (h0 : \[ForAll] t, t1 \[LessEqual] t \
\[RightArrow] F t 0 = eth j0 s 0 t) :\\n    \[ForAll] m t D R, t1 \
\[LessEqual] t \[RightArrow] 2 \[LessEqual] D \[RightArrow] Front F j0 s t D \
\[RightArrow] IsB F j0 s t D \[RightArrow] REdge F j0 s t R \[RightArrow]\\n  \
    R < D + 7 * m \[RightArrow]\\n      \[Exists] n, n < m \[And] \[Exists] \
D', Front F j0 s (t + n + 1) D' \[And] \[Not] IsB F j0 s (t + n + 1) D' \
